From 7bcfff710bb4eb6b65514ff1726cc5de8889368a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:21:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 002/106] pwm: Add an Allwinner A100 PWM driver

Add a driver for the PWM controller of the Allwinner A100/A133: plain PWM
output (cycle mode) on its 4 channels, clocked from the 24 MHz oscillator,
whose rate comes from the "hosc" clock.

The block has the register layout of the D1/T113 PWM, for which no driver
is in mainline, and not the one of the H616 PWM (pwm-sun8i, proposed
upstream), so neither can be reused. Periods and duty cycles are rounded
down as the PWM core expects (get_state() rounds up), the channel count
comes from the match data, and the channel clock is only set up when the
channel is off, so changing the duty cycle of a running channel does not
glitch the output.

Tested on the TrimUI Smart Pro (A133): the pwm-backlight on channel 0.

The clock source and divider (PCCR) are shared by a channel pair: they
are only programmed while both channels are off; otherwise the channel
uses the running sibling's setting (and refuses an APB1 source, whose
rate it does not know). get_state() takes the divider and the bypass
into account.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
---
